<title>POLAND: POLISH RAIL ENGINE DRIVERS MAY GO ON STRIKE.</title>
<headline>POLISH RAIL ENGINE DRIVERS MAY GO ON STRIKE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's rail engine drivers are considering launching an indefinite pay strike as of Sunday, the engine drivers' trade union said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Presently everything indicates there will be a protest,&quot; Jozef Smulski, the spokesman of the union, told Reuters. He added the union would make the final decision on the strike on Thursday.</p>
<p>The union wants the management of the State Railways (PKP) to keep real wages at the current levels and to increase employment.</p>
<p>The Solidarity trade union, which groups other PKP workers, will support the strike, said union's official Krzysztof Maminski.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
